From 524a931743f677af7436522df4c401ce1dbc8e62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michiel de Jong <michielbdejong@ontola.io>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:56:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Retain binary response snapshots across concurrent writes

Pin the immutable blob key while taking a fresh HTTP metadata snapshot, and reclaim retired versions only after their last response closes. Keep lazy blob I/O outside the metadata transaction and retirement guard, and leave write preconditions unchanged. Preserve stored non-RDF media parameters instead of dropping them.
---
